---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import ComingSoon from '../../components/ComingSoon.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Manufacturing — Use Case"
  description="Process-step verification — confirm each assembly step happened, in order, with timestamps."
  canonicalPath="/use-cases/manufacturing"
  mdTwin="/use-cases/manufacturing.md"
>
  <div class="page">
    <a class="back" href="/use-cases">← Use cases</a>
    <section class="hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">Manufacturing</p>
      <h1>Process-step verification</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Confirm each assembly step happened, in order, with timestamps.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="content">
      <p>
        Manufacturing quality control requires more than object detection — it requires
        temporal understanding. Did the torque wrench touch the bolt before the cover went
        on? Did the operator wear gloves during the chemical handling step? Were the
        components installed in the correct sequence? These are temporal questions that
        require a model that understands the video as a sequence of events, not a collection
        of frames.
      </p>
      <p>
        Darwin watches assembly line video and returns structured, timestamped verification
        results: which steps occurred, in what order, with what confidence. The outputs are
        deterministic — the same assembly footage produces the same verification report,
        making them auditable and legally defensible. Non-conformances come with timestamped
        evidence clips, ready for root cause analysis or regulatory documentation.
      </p>

      <ComingSoon note="Manufacturing process verification guide and integration examples — coming during our August launch." />
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .page { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 64px 24px 96px; }
  .back { font-size: var(--fs-body-sm); color: var(--color-text-muted); display: block; margin-bottom: 32px; }
  .back:hover { color: var(--color-signal); }
  .hero { margin-bottom: 40px; }
  .eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-footnote);
    font-weight: 500;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--color-signal);
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }
  h1 { font-size: var(--fs-h1); font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.02em; line-height: 1.2; margin: 0 0 16px; }
  .lede { font-size: var(--fs-body-lg); color: var(--color-text-muted); line-height: 1.6; margin: 0; }
  .content p { font-size: var(--fs-body-lg); line-height: 1.75; color: var(--color-text-primary); opacity: 0.85; margin: 0 0 16px; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) { h1 { font-size: var(--fs-h2); } .page { padding: 44px 20px 64px; } }
</style>
